# Template for .env (gitignored, same directory). deploy.sh creates .env from
# it on first start and asks for the database password - no need to copy it
# by hand.
#
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD: password of the database's `postgres` superuser - the
# one api/daemon log in with (as PSWD_DB, see docker-compose.yml) and the one
# clients (QGIS, pgAdmin, ...) use on localhost:DB_HOST_PORT. Postgres takes
# it only when the database is first created; to change it later, edit it
# here and deploy again (deploy.sh offers to apply it to the database).
# Written single-quoted by deploy.sh; may not contain a single quote.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
DB_USER=postgres
DB_NAME=hydrorisk
DB_HOST_PORT=5433
API_HOST_PORT=8001
